# Data & Model Integrity Principles

ProfitLens follows several principles throughout development:

### 1. No fabricated business data

Missing information will never be silently invented.

### 2. Evidence-backed insights

Important conclusions should be traceable to measurable data.

### 3. No unsupported precision

Predictions and recommendations should communicate uncertainty where appropriate.

### 4. Explainability

The system should be able to explain why an insight, prediction, or recommendation was produced.

### 5. Appropriate use of ML

Machine learning will only be used where it provides meaningful value over simpler analytical approaches.

### 6. Reproducibility

Data transformations, experiments, and model training should be reproducible.

### 7. Product-first architecture

Analytics, ML, GenAI, APIs, and visualization are components of one product rather than isolated projects.

